From 992fe54f771af4ab0f566b2a9b07cc19a0204c05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 14:02:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] escha vulkan: f16 activation staging - built, correct, and
 refuted; the real prefill win was the build

F16 STAGING, the lever the occupancy finding named. Shared memory halves at every rung (C16 8192 ->
4096 bytes) with f16 storage but the Hadamard butterfly kept in f32 registers - only the single
cross-subgroup step passes through f16, and acc[] stays f32 throughout. Correct on all 30 gate cases
in both arms. Measured, each arm a fresh process with its env printed from inside:
    staging off   pp512 22.57 / 22.42
    staging on    pp512 22.22 / 22.33
Flat. Halving shared memory did not buy occupancy here, so the occupancy ceiling is not set by the
staging array. Kept behind GGML_VK_ESCHA_F16_STAGE with the numbers at the switch.

THE ACTUAL WIN, found by accident. Prefill in BOTH arms measured ~22.4 against ~16.9 earlier the
same day. A binary saved before the cooperative-matrix reconfigure, run alternated against the
current one in one session, isolates it:
    pre-reconfigure   pp512 16.52 / 16.54
    current           pp512 25.41 / 24.87
+51% prefill from a build configuration defect. This build directory had been configured without
shader-extension detection and was missing SEVEN capabilities the GPU has: BFLOAT16, COOPMAT,
COOPMAT2, COOPMAT2_DECODE_VECTOR, FLOAT_E2M1, FLOAT_E4M3, INTEGER_DOT. Filed as F-137.

Scope measured rather than assumed: the estate engine of record is CLEAN. Huihui on
models/engines/arifi-b10524-union against the reconfigured fork engine reads 78.49 vs 77.57/79.80 -
equal. The defect was confined to this build directory, so nothing the President runs was affected.

The uncomfortable part, recorded because it changes how the rest of the day reads: every kernel A/B
before the reconfigure ran on the handicapped build. The verdicts survive - both arms always shared
one binary - but every absolute prefill number earlier in this lane is understated by roughly half.

TWO CONTAMINATION TRAPS PAID FOR, both of which produced confident wrong readings first:
- A build can silently omit a whole code path. The coopmat arm "gave nothing" twice before anyone
  noticed it had never been compiled in. Only an engagement probe that prints whether the arm ran
  caught it, and that probe stays.
- Environment set with $env: in one shell call persists into later calls in the same session. Two
  A/Bs were run with a stale variable pinning both arms to the same path. Benchmark arms now get a
  fresh process each and print the variable they claim to be testing.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Conflict-resolved: S4 split (f172be756): auto_split - our hunks re-homed into ggml-vulkan-types.h; wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS4_446.py)
